:: Farm Woodland
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "alex_farm">><<set $bus to "woodland">><<effects>>
<!-- OneDrive is ass btw its "backup files" cringe makes duplicates of all of your files and throws random VSCode
	errors on all of your files for code you already changed but wasn't "automatically" saved to the backups.
	Ended up moving most of my files on there into new folders with the exact same name and purpose. After doing
	that, errors be goned. Fuck that shit. -->
<<farm_work_update>>

You are in the woodland within the farm grounds.
<<if $farm_work.woodland is 0 >>
	Heavy branches and thick clumps of leaves litter the trails.
	<span class="red">You will not be able to forage.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 1>>
	Branches and leaves litter the trails.
	<span class="red">You will not be able to forage.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 2 and $farm.woodland is 2>>
	Only a few branches and sparse leaves cover the trails.
	You will be able to forage, <span class="yellow">although some branches may block your way.</span>
<<elseif $farm_work.woodland is 3 and $farm.woodland is 3>>
	You will be able to forage, <span class="green">and the paths through the woodland are clear.</span>
<</if>>

<<if Time.dayState is "night">>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		Snow weighs down the dark boughs above.
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		The trees shield you from the icy rain.
	<<else>>
		The chill night breeze is lessened here.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		Snow weighs down the boughs above.
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		The trees shield you from the worst of the rain.
	<<else>>
		You are surrounded by the chirping of birds.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $farm_work.pigs_out is 0>>
	<<if _farm_work_time <= -3>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are asleep in their sty.
	<<elseif _farm_work_time <= 0>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are rubbing each other awake.
	<<else>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> squeal to be let out.
	<</if>>
<<elseif $farm_work.pigs_out is 1>>
	<<if Time.season is "winter">>
		<span class="teal">The earth is too cold to find edible fungi.</span>
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
		<span class="teal">The <<farm_text_many pig>> stay away from the ice treeline.</span>
	<<elseif Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
		<span class="orange">The
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> pigpeople forage
			<<else>> pigs root
			<</if>>
			around in the muddy undergrowth.
		</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="orange">The
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>> pigpeople forage
			<<else>>pigs root
			<</if>>
			around in the damp undergrowth.
		</span>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _farm_work_time < 46>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> shuffle around in their sty.
		<!-- The pigs whisper to each other about a community of angry birds deep within the woodlands. About how the birds
			are constructing a giant slingshot to free their brethren. The pigs sound fearful. ++Stress -->
	<<else>>
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> are asleep in their sty.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<<if $farm_work.alex is "woodland">>
	Alex is removing dead wood.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $stress gte 10000>>
	<<passoutfarmroad>>
<<elseif $farm_attack_timer is 0 and Time.hour gte 21>>
	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	Alex rushes over. <span class="red">"Remy's here,"</span> <<he>> says. "We can do this. Go get ready, I'll
	<<if $farm.tower_guard>>
		check on $farm.tower_guard."
	<<else>>
		see if I can spot them."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<farm_assault_intro>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Prepare|Farm Assault Wardrobe]]>><<endevent>><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if $farm_work.alex is "woodland">>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to help Alex tend the woodland.
		<<else>>
			<<foresticon>><<link [[Help Alex tend the woodland (0:20)|Farm Woodland Tend Alex]]>><<set $farm_work.woodland += 1>><<farm_count 20>><<physique 2>><<pass 20>><<tending 2>><<tiredness 2>><<set $farm_work.tending += 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gtending>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<<elseif $farm_work.woodland lt $farm.woodland>>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to tend the woodland.
		<<else>>
			<<foresticon>><<link [[Tend the woodland (0:20)|Farm Woodland Tend]]>><<set $farm_work.woodland += 1>><<farm_count 20>><<physique 2>><<pass 20>><<tending 2>><<tiredness 2>><<set $farm_work.tending += 1>><</link>><<gtiredness>><<gtending>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<!-- The original code allowed you to forage once a day, regardless of the woodland's current tending status.
		I believe it would be better if you could only forage AFTER the woodlands have been fully tended to (Untidy
		woodlands = Hard to navigate). Since the "Forage for fungi" activity will also be a way to raise the Pig's Respect,
		I think it makes sense if the player has the option to forage once per day at Woodland Level 2, and twice per day
		at Woodland Level 3.
		
		If think it would be fair if a Level 3 Woodland still gives double the produce of a Level 2 Woodland, as it will
		need an extra 20 minutes of Tending each day and further increases that rate that the pigs lose Respect for the
		player. If the player doesn't want to spend that time tending, they can wait for Alex to finish it when he's doing
		his chores. However, the "Forage for fungi" activity will only be available while the pigs are out in their pen.
		
		It costs £30,000 to reach a Level 2 Woodland, and £80,000 to reach a Level 3 Woodland.
		
		Using the current Market Stall rates, Foraging for Fruit with a Level 2 Woodland will now give £100 worth of Fruit,
		while Foraging for Fungi will give £50-200 worth of Fungi, depending on the player's Athleticism and Tending skills.

		Foraging will be broken up into 3 20-minute events, where a dangerEvent() may trigger each time. When Foraging for
		fungi, there will be a 2/3 chance for a Pig-based Skill-Check. Passing this Skill Check will give +1 Pig's Respect.

		Foraging for Fungi will also require the player to reward the pigs when they return to the farm, either with ~£20
		worth of potatoes or carrots, or ~£4 worth of apples. The player can also choose the reward the pigs with their
		body. (1x Consensual Pig Encounters above -5 Pig's Respect, 2x Consensual Pig Encounters from -19 to -5 Pig's
		Respect, and 3x Consensual Pig Encounters at -20 Pig's Respect and below). These food rates are doubled for a
		Level 3 Woodland, and scale based on the combined market value of the Mushrooms and Truffles that have been
		harvested. 

		Rewarding the pigs in any way will give +3 Pig's Respect, while refusing will give -3 Pig's Respect.
		
		If the player refuses when the Pig's Respect is already less than or equal to -5, they will enter a Farm Pigs Feed
		extreme encounter. The player can call for Alex's Help, or try to pass the Skill Check for +1 Pig's Respect. Losing
		the combat encounter will also cause the pigs to take HALF of the player's harvest.
		
		If the Pig's Respect is less than or equal to -20, the Tending / Physique checks will become much harder (50%
		chance at maximum Tending, 75% chance at 15,000 Physique), and they will first lead the player deep into the
		woodlands so the player can't call Alex for help. The player will be unable to satiate them with regular food, as
		the pigs demand an immediate reward. The player's only non-Skill-based options will be to give them half of the
		player's harvest or to reward them with their body. Losing a combat encounter will also cause the pigs to take ALL
		of the PC's harvest.

		The dangerEvent()'s that can be obtained when Foraging for fungi will be 1/3 generic, and 2/3 Pig-based. That means
		the player, if they have maximum Allure and reward the pigs each time, will be able to gain ~5 Pig's Respect every
		time they Forage for fungi. With a Level 3 Woodland, they can theoretically raise the Pig's Respect by 10 each day.

		Assuming the player rewards the pigs with potatoes or carrots, and the Pig's Respect is above -20, a Level 3
		Woodland will give around £800 - £80 = £720 per day, for 2 hours of work (If Alex tends the woodlands for you).

		See "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/11sYCs887BkfBjLbs5lufGH1KH-4Y5FK-UFpixTKyT4Y" for the exact math. -->
	<<if $farm_work.forage lt ($farm.woodland - 1) and $farm_work.woodland is $farm.woodland>>
		<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
			<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to forage.
		<<else>>
			<<foresticon "bush">><<link [[Forage for fruits (1:00)|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><<set $farm_work.forage += 1>>
				<<tiredness 2>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: [0, 0, 0],
					remainingAttempts: 3,
					forageType: "fruit",
					}>>
			<</link>><<gtiredness>>
			<<if $farm_work.pigs_out is 1 and Time.season is not "winter">>
				<br>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Forage for fungi (1:00)|Farm Woodland Forage]]>><<set $farm_work.forage += 1>>
					<<tiredness 2>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: [0, 0, 0],
						remainingAttempts: 3,
						forageType: "fungi",
						}>>
				<</link>><<gtiredness>>
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:05)|Farm Work]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Tend
<<effects>><<outfitChecks>>

You remove dead wood, and trim the branches of the wildest trees.
<br><br>

<<if dangerEvent()>>
	<!-- 0 means upper clothing, 1 means lower clothing -->
	<<set _branchTarget to random(0, 1)>>
	<<if _top>>
		<<set _top.integrity -= 10>>
		<<if _top.integrity lte 0>>
			Your _top.name <<= $_top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
			<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undertop>>.</span>
		<<else>>
			Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch, leaving _top.name worse for wear.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _bottom.name isnot "naked">>
		<<set _bottom.integrity -= 10>>
		<<if _bottom.integrity lte 0>>
			Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
			<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undies>>.</span>
		<<else>>
			Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on one such branch, leaving _bottom.name worse for wear.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		A gust of wind animates the branches as you work, scratching your skin.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
	<</if>>
	<<integritycheck no_text>><<exposure>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Alex
<<effects>>

<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
You help Alex remove dead wood, and trim the branches of the wildest trees.
<br><br>

<<if random(1, 4) is 4>>
	<<He>> points at the boughs above. "We'll need help to reach," <<he>> says. "I'll fetch it."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> returns a few moments later, carrying a long ladder beneath one arm. <<He>> rests it against the offending tree.

	<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
		"The ground's uneven. You climb with the saw, and I'll steady you. Shouldn't take long."
		<br><br>

		<<if setup.clothes.lower[clothesIndex('lower', $worn.lower)].skirt is 1>>
			You climb the ladder. It wobbles a little, and you hesitate.
			<br><br>

			"You alright?" Alex says.
			<br>
			You nod, and reach for the nearest branch. You rest the saw against it, then run the metal back and forth. You pick up speed. The force reverberates through you, rocking the ladder a little.
			<br>
			A stiff breeze ruffles your skirt, brushing it against your legs.
			<br>
			You glance down, <span class="pink">and catch Alex staring right between your thighs.</span> <<His>> cheeks are red.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Ignore|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Ignore]]>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Alex lust 10>><<arousal 1000>><</link>><<ggarousal>><<gstress>><<gglust>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Call out|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Call]]>><<stress -6>><<npcincr Alex love -1>><</link>><<llove>><<lstress>>
			<br>
			<<if hasSexStat("exhibitionism", 3)>>
				<<link [[Flaunt|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Flaunt]]>><</link>><<exhibitionist3>><<npcincr Alex lust 5>>
				<br>
			<</if>>
			<<if displayDefiantOption(500)>>
				<<link [[Taunt|Farm Woodland Tend Alex Taunt]]>><<wolfDefiant 500>><<def 1>><</link>><<npcincr Alex dom -3>><<npcincr Alex lust 5>><<defianttext 500>><<lldom>><<glust>>
				<br>
			<</if>>

		<<else>>
			You climb the ladder. It wobbles a little, and you hesitate.
			<br><br>

			"You alright?" Alex says.
			<br>
			You nod, and reach for the nearest branch. You rest the saw against it, then run the metal back and forth. You pick up speed. The force reverberates through you, rocking the ladder a little.
			<br>
			You give Alex a heads up. The branch falls to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
			<br><br>

			"Thanks for the help," Alex says as you reach the bottom.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"The ground's uneven. Could you hold the ladder while I climb? It shouldn't take long."
		<br><br>

		You stand at the base of the ladder as <<he>> climbs.
		<<if $pronoun is "f">>
			You wouldn't need to lean much to see up <<his>> skirt.
			<br><br>

			<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to 700>>
			<<link [[Peek|Farm Woodland Tend Skirt]]>><<arousal 600>><</link>><<skulduggerydifficulty>><<garousal>>
			<br>
			<<link [[Don't peek|Farm Woodland Tend No Skirt]]>><<npcincr Alex love 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			You keep your face down to shield yourself from the splinters. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. The branch falls to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
			<br><br>

			"Thanks for the help," Alex says as <<he>> reaches the bottom.<<glove>><<npcincr Alex love 1>>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Skirt
<<effects>>

You step around the ladder just as a gust billows Alex's skirt, giving you a clear view of <<his>> red boyshorts.
<br><br>

<<skulduggerycheck>>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>

	<<He>> doesn't notice your gaze. You continue stealing peeks as Alex saws the branch. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. The branch thuds to the leaf-strewn floor beside you. "Coming down."
	<br><br>

	<<skulduggeryuse>>

	"Thanks for the help," <<he>> says once down.<<glove>><<npcincr Alex love 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

<<else>>

	<<He>> glances down, <span class="red">and yelps.</span> <<He>> pushes <<his>> skirt between <<his>> thighs with one hand, and almost falls from the ladder.<<llove>><<gglust>><<npcincr Alex love -1>><<npcincr Alex lust 10>>
	<br><br>

	"D-don't look," <<he>> says.

	<<skulduggeryuse>>

	<<link [[Apologise|Farm Woodland Tend Apologise]]>><<npcincr Alex love 1>><<stress 6>><</link>><<gstress>><<glove>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Tease|Farm Woodland Tend Tease]]>><<npcincr Alex dom 1>><</link>><<promiscuous1>><<gdom>>

<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Apologise
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"I-I'm so sorry," you say, averting your eyes. "I didn't mean to look."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Yeah, that was classless of me," you say, averting your eyes. "Sorry."
<<else>>
	"Sorry," you say, averting your eyes. "That was rude of me."
<</if>>
<br><br>

"Just don't look again," Alex says. <<He>> saws through the log, but keeps <<his>> legs together until <<hes>> finished.
<br><br>

<<Hes>> still blushing when the branch falls to the floor, and <<he>> climbs back down.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend Tease
<<effects>>

<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	"C-cute underwear," you giggle.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Nice underwear," you tease. "Shame to hide it."
<<else>>
	"You've good taste in underwear," you say.
<</if>>
<<promiscuity1>>

Alex's blush deepens. <<He>> continues sawing the log, but keeps <<his>> legs tight together, <<his>> skirt bunched between them, until <<hes>> finished.
<br><br>

<<Hes>> still blushing when the branch falls to the floor, and <<he>> climbs back down.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Tend No Skirt
<<effects>>

You look away as Alex saws through the branch. "Here it comes," <<he>> says. It thuds to the leaf-strewn floor a moment later.
<br><br>

"Thanks for the help," <<he>> says as <<he>> reaches the bottom.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Farm Woodland Forage
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts - 1>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<effects>><<outfitChecks>>

<<farm_gen pig>>

<<if _remainingAttempts lt 0>>
	<!-- Triggers at the end of the foraging session -->
	<<if _forageType is "fruit" or $farm.beasts.pigs gte -20>>
		You can see the treeline from here.

		<<set _uniqueItems to 0>>
		<<for _i = 0; _i lt _basket.length; _i++>>
			<<if _basket[_i] gt 0>>
				<<set _uniqueItems += 1>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>
		<<if _forageType is "fruit">>
			<<set _basketTypes to ["strawberry", "peach", "plum"]>>
			You have found
			<span class="green">
				<<for _j = 0; _j < 3; _j++>>
					<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
						<<if _basket[_j] gt 0>>
							<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>.
						<</if>>
					<<elseif _basket[_j] gt 0 and _j + 1 < _uniqueItems>>
						<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>,
					<<else>>
						and <<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>.
					<</if>>
				<</for>>
			</span>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
			<br>
		<<elseif _forageType is "fungi">>
			<<set _basketTypes to ["mushroom", "truffle", ""]>>
			You have found
			<span class="green">
				<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
					<<for _j = 0; _j < 2; _j++>>
						<<if _basket[_j] gt 0>>
							<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>.
						<</if>>
					<</for>>
				<<else>>
					<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" _basket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" _basket[1] "truffle">>.
				<</if>>
			</span>
			<br><br>

			<!-- The base foraging rates will require you to reward £100.00 of fungi with £8.00 of potatoes, £10.00
				of carrots, or £5.00 of apples. This assumes apples can only be harvested in the Forest. Quantities
				will need to be changed if apples suddenly become easier to harvest.
				
				The requested quantity is increased by 100% if the Pig's Respect is between -19 and -5. -->
			<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
				<<set _respectModifier to 1>>
				The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you.
				<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"Reward?" "Helpful?" "Food?" "Reward?" They ask.
				<<else>>They bump you with their snouts, asking for a reward.
				<</if>>
				While you could also give them nothing, you get the feeling that refusing too often may be a
				<span class="red">very bad idea.</span>
			<<else>>
				<<set _respectModifier to 2>>
				The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you. They jostle you around, insisting on a large reward.
				While you could also give them nothing, you get the feeling that refusing any more
				<span class="red">will be a very bad idea.</span>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<!-- Truffles are significantly more expensive than mushrooms. To prevent truffles from being weighted
				much more heavily than mushrooms in the request calculations, the Pigs will now adjust their requests
				according to the QUANTITY of each item that's been collected, scaled by the average value the player
				expects to make each hour. -->
			<<set _averageValue to (2 * setup.foodstuff["mushroom"].shop.sell_price
				+ 1 * setup.foodstuff["truffle"].shop.sell_price) / 3>>
			<!-- Units are in hundredths of a pound. Quantities are rounded up because pigs are greedy. -->
			<<set _requestedValue to _basket[0] * _averageValue + _basket[1] * _averageValue>>
			<!-- Requires 8% of the market value in potatoes. -->
			<<set _requiredPotatoes to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.08 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["potato"].shop.sell_price)>>
			<!-- Or, 10% of the market value in carrots. -->
			<<set _requiredCarrots to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.10 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["wild_carrot"].shop.sell_price)>>
			<!-- Or, 5% of the market value in apples. -->
			<<set _requiredApples to Math.ceil((_requestedValue * 0.05 * _respectModifier)
				/ setup.foodstuff["apple"].shop.sell_price)>>
			
			<!-- Respect gains will be added up at the end, and will not be shown in the links to avoid clutter. -->
			<<if $farm_work.pigs_fed gte 6>>
				<<foodstufficon "potato">><span class="blue">The pigs are too full to want more potatoes.</span>
			<<elseif $foodstuff["potato"].amount gte _requiredPotatoes>>
				<<foodstufficon "potato">><<link [[Reward them with potatoes (0:20)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>><<set $phase to "potato">>
					<<set $phase to {
						type: "potato",
						quantity: _requiredPotatoes
					}>>
					<<set $foodstuff["potato"].amount -= _requiredPotatoes>>
				<</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "potatoes to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'potato'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if $foodstuff["wild_carrot"].amount gte _requiredCarrots>>
				<<foodstufficon "wild_carrot">><<link [[Reward them with carrots (0:10)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						type: "carrot",
						quantity: _requiredCarrots
					}>>
					<<set $foodstuff["wild_carrot"].amount -= _requiredCarrots>>
				<</link>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "carrots to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'wild_carrot'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if $foodstuff["apple"].amount gte _requiredApples>>
				<<if currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400 and $mathstrait gte 3>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:20)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $phase to {
							type: "apple",
							quantity: _requiredApples
						}>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<<elseif currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:15)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $phase to {
							type: "apple",
							quantity: _requiredApples
						}>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<<else>>
					<<foodstufficon "apple">><<link [[Reward them with apples (0:10)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
						<<set $phase to {
							type: "apple",
							quantity: _requiredApples
						}>>
						<<set $foodstuff["apple"].amount -= _requiredApples>>
					<</link>>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<<insufficientQuantity "apples to satisfy them" "blue" "<<foodstufficon 'apple'>>">>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			
			<<if ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster) and hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Reward them with your body|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						type: "body",
						quantity: 0
					}>>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<getouticon>><<link [[Reward them with nothing|Farm Woodland Forage Reward]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					type: "nothing",
					quantity: 0
				}>>
			<</link>><<llrespect>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<!-- A player with Tending S, the Green Thumb trait, and a Level 3 Woodland
			can find an average of:
			20 * 3 * 2.4 = 144 fungi each time they enter the Woodland.

			Once the Pig's Respect is less than -20, they will take the player deep
			into the woodland at the end of the foraging session, and demand a
			reward. The player will have the option to give them their harvest,
			reward them with their body, or refuse.

			The pigs will initially want to have sex with the player 4 times
			(pigsLeft will be 4). If the player offers them their harvest, each
			pigsLeft will try to eat a random(20, 40) amount of fungi from the
			player's basket, repeating 5 times (150 fungi on average). Each fully
			satisfied attempt will reduce pigsLeft by 1. If the pigs can eat their
			fill at least 4 times, they will leave the player alone.

			If the pigs can eat their fill 5 times, they will leave the player with
			whatever food is left over, then rest and head back to the farm.

			Each fully satisfied pig gives +1 Pig's Respect (+4 max).

			Pigs will eat the truffles first, then the mushrooms.

			If the player refuses, pigsLeft will increase by 1, and all remaining
			encounters will become non-consensual.

			See:
			"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/11sYCs887BkfBjLbs5lufGH1KH-4Y5FK-UFpixTKyT4Y"
			for the exact math.
			-->
		You've been here for a while. You decide to count up your harvest, then head back towards the farm.

		<<set _uniqueItems to 0>>
		<<for _i = 0; _i lt _basket.length; _i++>>
			<<if _basket[_i] gt 0>>
				<<set _uniqueItems += 1>>
			<</if>>
		<</for>>

		<<set _basketTypes to ["mushroom", "truffle", ""]>>
		You have found
		<span class="green">
			<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
				<<for _j = 0; _j < 2; _j++>>
					<<if _basket[_j] gt 0>>
						<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>.
					<</if>>
				<</for>>
			<<else>>
				<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" _basket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" _basket[1] "truffle">>.
			<</if>>
		</span>
		<br><br>

		You look around. You don't recognize this area of the woods. Something isn't right...
		<br><br>

		<!-- The farm_gen chain of doom -->
		A <<farm_text pig>> pokes <<farm_his pig>> head out from behind a tree.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> walks out from a bush.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> appears behind you.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> pushes through a thicket.
		<<farm_gen pig>>
		You see another <<farm_text pig>>.
		And then another. And another. And another. And another. <span class="red">And another. And another.</span>
		<br><br>
		
		The <<farm_text_many pig>> surround you.

		<<farm_gen pig>>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			One of the <<farm_text_many pig>> speaks up. "We help you. Many time. You give reward. Now."
		<<else>>
			They stare at your basket. You think the implication is clear.
		<</if>>
		You could give them your harvest, but money is tight and you were going to sell it on the market.
		<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>> You could offer them your body, but how many times will you need to satisfy them?<</if>>
		You hesitate.
		<br><br>

		<<foodstufficon "mushroom">><<link [[Offer your harvest (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
			<<set $phase to {
				type: "basket",
				basket: _basket
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
		
		<!-- The "body" and "nothing" rewards are disabled when bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters. -->
		<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<animalicon "pig">><<link [[Offer your body (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						type: "body",
						basket: _basket
					}>>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<foresticon>><<link [[Refuse (?:??)|Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					type: "nothing",
					basket: _basket
				}>>
			<</link>><<dangerousText>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<pass 20>>
	
	<<pigsOpinion>>

	<<if _forageType is "fruit">>
		You take a basket into the woodland, and search the boughs and bushes for fruit.
	<<elseif _forageType is "fungi">>
		You take a basket into the woodland, and search the undergrowth for fungi.
		<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -20>>
			The <<farm_text_many pig>> guide you along.
		<<else>>
			<span class="red">The <<farm_text_many pig>> guide you along.</span>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
	<</if>>
	<<physique 1>>
	<br><br>
	<!-- Changed the RNG checks so that the player makes 3 foraging checks, each taking 20 minutes,
		with a chance of receiving ANY type of fruit.
		
		Basket holds Strawberries, Peaches, and Plums when foraging for fruit, or Mushrooms and
		Truffles when foraging for fungi. When foraging for fungi, the last index is not used. -->	
	<<if _forageType is "fruit">>
		<<set _target to random(0, 2)>>
		<<switch _target>>
			<<case 0>>
				<!-- Strawberries -->
				<<wearProp "strawberry basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "strawberry">> strawberries.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick strawberry 20 50>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick strawberry 10 25>>
				<</if>>
				<<set _basket[0] += _tending_amount>>
			<<case 1>>
				<!-- Peaches -->
				<<wearProp "peach basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "peach">> peaches.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick peach 10 40>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick peach 5 20>>
				<</if>>
				<<set _basket[1] += _tending_amount>>
			<<case 2>>
				<!-- Plums -->
				<<wearProp "plum basket">>
				<span class="green">You find some ripe <<foodstufficon "plum">> plums.</span>
				<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
					<<tending_pick plum 20 40>>
				<<else>>
					<<tending_pick plum 10 20>>
				<</if>>
				<<set _basket[2] += _tending_amount>>
		<</switch>>
	<<elseif _forageType is "fungi">>
		<!-- When foraging for fungi, there is a 2/3 chance to find Mushrooms, and a 1/3 chance to find Truffles -->
		<<set _target to random(1, 3)>>
		<!-- For calculation purposes, the exact quantities and frequencies that the Mushrooms and Truffles are
			harvested at should stay equal to each other if they end up being adjusted. Otherwise, the _averageValue
			variable will need to be recalculated with the new values in mind. -->
		<<if _target lte 2>>
			<!-- Mushrooms -->
			<<wearProp "mushroom basket">>
			<span class="green">You find some <<foodstufficon "mushroom">> mushrooms.</span>
			<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
				<<tending_pick mushroom 10 30>>
			<<else>>
				<<tending_pick mushroom 5 15>>
			<</if>>
			<<set _basket[0] += _tending_amount>>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Truffles -->
			<!-- NOTE: THERE DOES NOT CURRENTLY EXIST A TRUFFLE BASKET SPRITE. SPRITEWORK NEEDED. -->
			<<wearProp "mushroom basket">>
			<span class="green">You find some <<foodstufficon "truffle">> truffles.</span>
			<<if $farm.woodland gte 3>>
				<<tending_pick truffle 10 30>>
			<<else>>
				<<tending_pick truffle 5 15>>
			<</if>>
			<<set _basket[1] += _tending_amount>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Forage): forageType is invalid. Please report.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<!-- If the player is foraging for fruit or disabled bestiality, they will get scratched by
		some branches and nothing else will happen.

		If they are foraging for fungi with a Level 2 Woodland, they will have a 1/2 chance of
		getting molested by a pig after being scratched by a branch.
		
		If they are foraging for fungi with a Level 3 Woodland, they will have a 4/5 chance of
		getting molested by a pig.
		
		If the chosen target on the player's body fails, or if the player gets hit with an
		unlucky 1/4, they will fall to the ground and the skill checks will be harder. -->
	<<if (_forageType is "fruit" and dangerEvent()) or
		(_forageType is "fungi" and ((_checkResults[0] is 2 and _checkResults[1] is 2) or dangerEvent(1.25)))>>
		<<set _woodlandFungiChecks to [
			{checkType: "hairlength", checkMin: 300, checkMax: 500},
			{checkType: "uppernaked", checkFail: true},
			{checkType: "lowernaked", checkFail: true}
		]>>
		<<eventChecks _woodlandFungiChecks false>>
		<<set _attemptOne to random(0, 2)>>

		<<if _attemptOne is 0 and _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2>>
			Your <<hairDetails>> catches on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it. It's stuck.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
		<<elseif _attemptOne is 1 and _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2>>
			<<set _top.integrity -= 10>>
			<<if _top.integrity lte 0>>
				Your _top.name <<= $_top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
				<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undertop>>.</span>
			<<else>>
				Your _top.name <<= _top.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch, leaving _top.name worse for wear.
			<</if>>
		<<elseif _attemptOne is 2 and _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2>>
			<<set _bottom.integrity -= 10>>
			<<if _bottom.integrity lte 0>>
				Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch as a gust of wind disturbs it.
				<span class="pink">The force tears the fabric from your body, baring your <<undies>>.</span>
			<<else>>
				Your _bottom.name <<= _bottom.plural ? "catch" : "catches">> on a branch, leaving _bottom.name worse for wear.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			A gust of wind animates the nearby branches, scratching your skin.<<gpain>><<pain 4>>
		<</if>>
		<<integritycheck no_text>><<exposure>>
		<br><br>
		
		<<if _forageType is "fungi" and (($farm.woodland is 2 and random(1, 2) is 2)
			or ($farm.woodland is 3 and random(1, 5) is lte 4))
			and ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
			<!-- The event will be initiated by the player's hair or clothes catching on a branch. Upon triggering
				this event, a pig will try to molest them.
				
				If however the targeted check fails, due to the player's hair being too short, the
				player's upper or lower clothing slot being naked, or they simply hit the unlucky 1/4, they will
				first fall the the ground and the skill checks will be harder. -->
			<<if _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2 and random(1, 4) is not 4>>
				<<if _attemptOne is 0>>
					As you untangle your hair,
				<<else>>
					<!-- Player's body is targeted while they're wearing clothes. -->
					As you untangle yourself,
				<</if>>
				
				<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
					a <<farm_text pig>> grasps your <<hairDetails>> and tries to force you to the ground.
				<<else>>
					a pig rears on its hind legs and tries to force you to the ground.
				<</if>>
				<br><br>

				<<link [[Scold|Farm Woodland Pigs Scold]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType,
						startPosition: "standing"
					}>>
				<</link>><<tendingdifficulty 1 900>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Shove <<farm_him pig>> away|Farm Woodland Pigs Shove]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType,
						startPosition: "standing"
					}>>
				<</link>><<physiquedifficulty 1 13500>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Endure|Farm Woodland Pigs Endure]]>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<farm_pigs -1>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType,
						startPosition: "standing"
					}>>
				<</link>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<lrespect>>
				<br>
				<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 3)>>
					<<link [[Give <<farm_him pig>> a hand|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
						<<set $phase to {
							basket: _basket,
							remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
							forageType: _forageType,
							startPosition: "standing"
						}>>
					<</link>><<deviant3>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				<<if _attemptOne is 0 and _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2>>
					<!-- Unlucky 1/4. -->
					As you untangle your hair,
				<<elseif (_attemptOne is 1 or _attemptOne is 2) and _checkResults[_attemptOne] is 2>>
					<!-- Unlucky 1/4. -->
					As you untangle yourself,
				<<else>>
					<!-- Failed the check. -->
					As you back away from the branches,
				<</if>>
				you trip on a root and fall onto your back. Looking up, you see a <<farm_text pig>> standing in
				front of you. Emboldened by your vulnerability, <<farm_he pig>> tries to mount you.
				<br><br>

				<!-- Exact position is "missionary". -->
				<<link [[Scold|Farm Woodland Pigs Scold]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType,
						startPosition: "prone"
					}>>
				<</link>><<tendingdifficulty 1 1200>>
				<br>
				<<link [[Shove <<farm_him pig>> away|Farm Woodland Pigs Shove]]>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType,
						startPosition: "prone"
					}>>
				<</link>><<physiquedifficulty 1 16000>>
				<br>
				<!-- Enduring not possible because the player is already prone. -->
				<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 4)>>
					<<link [[Give <<farm_him pig>> a hand|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
						<<set $phase to {
							basket: _basket,
							remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
							forageType: _forageType,
							startPosition: "prone"
						}>>
					<</link>><<deviant4>>
					<br>
				<</if>>
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
					forageType: _forageType
				}>>
			<</link>>
		<</if>>

	<<else>>
		<!-- Ok ok. Hear me out. *Dons tinfoil hat* WHAT IF. Huamns are not the only ones who gain benefits from using
			the Strange Flowers? WHAT IF. Animals who eat them gain a minor boost to their intelligence, and increased
			lust towards humans? WHAT IF. The pigs on Alex's Farm started eating these after being let into the
			Woodland, WHICH ENDED UP MAKING THEM SMARTER?!!?? AM I COOKING?!?! DO WE COOK THESE??!!?? -->
		<<if random(1, 5) is 1>>
			You smell a mesmerising sweetness. It leads you to a patch of strange purple flowers.
			<br><br>
			<<if pcAreArmsBound("both")>>
				<!-- Shouldn't currently be possible to reach this text, as you can't start foraging if your arms are
					bound. Maybe there will be an arm binding event in the future? -->
				<span class="red">Both of your arms are bound</span>, so you are unable to pick the flower.
				<br>
			<<else>>
				<<foodstufficon "strange_flower">><<link [[Pick|Farm Woodland Strange Harvest]]>><<drugs 60>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
						forageType: _forageType
					}>>
				<</link>><<garousal>>
			<</if>>
			<br>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Ignore|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
					forageType: _forageType
				}>>
			<</link>>
			<br>

		<<else>>
			<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
					forageType: _forageType
				}>>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


<!-- rewardType can be "basket", "body", or "nothing" -->
<!-- Reward Tradeoffs:
	Basket:
		Pros: Reduces the number of pigs the player needs to have sex with.
			With enough mushrooms, the sex can be avoided entirely.
			Each satisfied pig gives +1 Respect.
		Cons: The pigs demand a LOT of mushrooms.
			The number of pigs is decreased for each pig that is FULLY satisfied.
	Body:
		Pros: Pigs will not steal from your basket while you're having sex.
			Each satisfied pig gives +1 Respect.
			You are having sex with pigs.
		Cons: You are having sex with pigs.
	Nothing:
		Pros: Encounters will all be non-consensual. You're such a go go getter lmao
			Each pig fought off gives +1 Respect.
			This is technically the option that gives you the maximum amount of Pig's Respect (By fighting off 5 pigs).
		Cons: Pigs will steal from your basket while you're being raped.
			1 more pig will try to rape you.
	--> 
:: Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme
<<set _rewardType to $phase.type>>
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<effects>><<outfitChecks>>

<<if _rewardType is "basket">>
	You hold out your basket. The <<farm_text_many pig>> stare at it.
	<br><br>

	<<farm_gen pig>>

	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"I-I hope this is enough for you." You start handing out your mushrooms. "Eep!" But a <<farm_text pig>> knocks your
		basket out of your hands.
		<!-- Lillia transformation when? Plz I need -->
		<<if _basket[1] gt 0>>They dig through the spilled contents, seeming to like your truffles.
		<<else>>They dig into the spilled contents, pulling back after grabbing a mouthful of mushroom.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		You stare back at them. They start back at you. Finally, you sigh. "Ugh. Fine." You dump your basket into the grass.
		<<if _basket[1] gt 0>>They start picking through your harvest, seeming to like your truffles.
		<<else>>They start picking out what they like, taking away your mushrooms one by one.
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		"Is this enough?" you ask them. You pour out your harvest in front of them.
		<<if _basket[1] gt 0>>They consider it, then start grabbing from the spread. They like your truffles.
		<<else>>They consider it, then start grabbing from the spread. The largest mushrooms are the first to go.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _pigsUnsatisfied to -1>>
	<<for _i = 0; _i < 5; _i++>>
		<<set _amountTaken to random(20, 40)>>
		<!-- Take from truffles if they exist -->
		<<if _basket[1] gt 0 and _basket[1] gte _amountTaken>>
			<<set _basket[1] -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to 0>>
		<!-- Empty the truffles if there aren't enough -->
		<<elseif _basket[1] gt 0 and _basket[1] lt _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to _amountTaken - _basket[1]>>
			<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= _basket[1]>>
			<<set _basket[1] to 0>>
		<</if>>
		<!-- Take from mushrooms if they exist. Can use an "if" statement here because the pig will either be fully
			satisfied by the truffles (0), or the truffles will run out and cause the pig to look for mushrooms
			instead (> 0) -->
		<<if _basket[0] gt 0 and _basket[0] gte _amountTaken>>
			<<set _basket[0] -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to 0>>
		<<elseif _basket[0] gt 0 and _basket[0] lt _amountTaken>>
			<<set _amountTaken to _amountTaken - _basket[0]>>
			<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= _basket[0]>>
			<<set _basket[0] to 0>>
		<</if>>

		<!-- Check if the pig was fully satisfied. -->
		<<if _amountTaken gt 0>>
			<<set _pigsUnsatisfied += 1>>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Each serving of fungi takes the pigs ~2 minutes to eat. -->
			<<pass 2>>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>

	<!-- Players who've disabled bestiality can only get a little respect. Failing to satisfy the pigs will instead give them
		increasing amounts of trauma, stress, and pain.

		The pigs will take 30-40 minutes to return to the farm from where they took the player.
		When satisfied, they will rest for 10 minutes before leaving. -->
	<<if _pigsUnsatisfied lte 0 or not ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
		<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
		<<pass _passTime>>

		<<if _pigsUnsatisfied lte 0>>
			<<pass 10>>
			After some time, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze on the earth, satisfied with the meal.
			<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				<<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 4>>
			<<else>>
				<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		
			<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0>>
				You pick up your basket. It seems like they left some food behind. After picking up their leftovers, you're
				able to find 
				<span class="green">
					<<if _uniqueItems is 1>>
						<<for _j = 0; _j < 2; _j++>>
							<<if _basket[_j] gt 0>>
								<<foodstuffReport _basketTypes[_j] _basket[_j] _basketTypes[_j]>>.
							<</if>>
						<</for>>
					<<else>>
						<<foodstuffReport "mushroom" _basket[0] "mushroom">>, and <<foodstuffReport "truffle" _basket[1] "truffle">>.
					<</if>>
				</span>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this
			time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle for the meal.
			<<if $settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes, but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from
				approaching.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span><<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Thank meal," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _pigsUnsatisfied is lte 2>>
			<!-- Should only be possible if bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters.
			Text for 1-2 unsatisfied pigs. -->
			<<pass 4>>
			Once your basket is empty, some <<farm_text_many pig>> lay on the earth, satisfied with their meal.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this
			time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, some of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They
			push you around, checking if you have any more food hidden away.<<gtrauma>><<gstress>>
			<!-- This amount includes the "It seems they think you've paid your due" stress, and adds +6 stress for every
				unsatisfied pig. -->
			<<trauma 6>>
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 1>><<stress 12>><<else>><<stress 18>><</if>>
			<br><br>

			Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Should only be possible if bestiality is disabled and the pigs aren't monsters.
			Text for 3-4 unsatisfied pigs. -->
			<<pass 2>>
			Once your basket is empty, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> lay down. However, most of them are unsatisfied.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, and you're worried about disturbing them, so you sit with your back against a tree. The
			<<farm_text_many pig>> get back up. However, instead of dispersing, they turn to you. They want more food.
			<br><br>

			<!-- Pigs may tear off player's clothes looking for more food. However, they will not try to molest the player. -->
			They knock you around, searching for anything you might have hidden away.
			<<if _top or _bottom>>
				They grasp and tear, and soon have your <span class="pink">clothes reduced to tatters.</span><<clothesruined>>
				<<ggtrauma>><<ggstress>><<gpain>><<pain 6>>
			<<else>>
				You trip and stumble as you're shoved, scraping your skin against the nearby trees.
				<<ggtrauma>><<ggstress>><<gpain>><<pain 12>>
			<</if>>
			<<trauma 12>>
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 3>><<stress 24>><<else>><<stress 30>><</if>>
			<br><br>

			Eventually, they tire of their search and trot away with a huff. You watch their outlines fade between the trees.
			Hesitantly, you follow them.
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<!-- Should only be possible if bestiality is enabled, or the pigs are monsters. -->
		<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 1>>
			<<pass 6>>
			After emptying your basket, most of the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze on the earth, satisfied with their meal.
			<<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 3>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this
			time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They
			walk up to you in a small group, intent on something more. 
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Not be rough," one of the <<farm_text_many pig>> says. "You give good food."
			<<else>>
				The others glance at them, then go back to lazing around.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<<elseif _pigsUnsatisfied is 2 or _pigsUnsatisfied is 3>>
			<<pass 4>>
			Once your basket is empty, some <<farm_text_many pig>> lay on the earth, satisfied with their meal.<<grespect>>
			<<if _pigsUnsatisfied is 2>><<farm_pigs 2>><<else>><<farm_pigs 1>><</if>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this
			time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle as thanks. However, some of the <<farm_text_many pig>> seem unsatisfied. They
			circle around you, intent on something more. 
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Not give enough," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "But okay. We less hungry."
			<<else>>
				The others glance at them, watching how you react.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<<pass 2>>
			Once your basket is empty, a few of the <<farm_text_many pig>> lay down. However, most of them are unsatisfied.
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, and you're worried about disturbing them, so you sit with your back against a tree. The
			<<farm_text_many pig>> get back up. However, instead of dispersing, they turn to you. They want something more. 
			<br><br>

			<<farm_gen pig>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"Give too little," a <<farm_text_many pig>> says. "Very little. Still hungry. You satisfy."
			<<else>>
				You can tell they're still hungry. They look at you with lust.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<!-- After feeding them, the player will have the option to have consensual or non-consensual sex with the pigs that
			are unsatisfied. Deviancy check for consensual sex will be lower since the player already fed them. -->
		<<if hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
			<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					rewardHelpful: false,
					helpfulPigGender: "m",
					currentConsensual: true,
					pigsLeft: _pigsUnsatisfied,
					demeanor: "submissive",
					location: "woodland",
					trueConsensual: false
				}>>
			<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: false,
				helpfulPigGender: "m",
				currentConsensual: false,
				pigsLeft: _pigsUnsatisfied,
				demeanor: "defiant",
				location: "woodland",
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

<<elseif _rewardType is "body">>
	<!-- Player will satisfy a pig with their body (+1 Pig's Respect). If the player has good Science and Tending,
		they will recognize and reward a pig that was particularly helpful (+1 Pig's Respect). -->
	You look among the <<farm_text_many pig>> gathered before you, deciding which one you'll offer your body to.
	<br><br>

	<!-- Player should have a 50% of passing the Science check with a Science Grade of A. -->
	<<set _rewardBodyChecks to [
		{checkType: "science", checkMin: 600, checkMax: 800},
		{checkType: "tending", checkMin: 600, checkMax: 800, includeBurden: false}
	]>>
	<<eventChecks _rewardBodyChecks>>
	<!-- Going to hell for this lol -->
	<<if _checkResults[0] is 2 and _checkResults[1] is 2>>
		<!-- Extra point of Respect if the player passes both checks. Passing this also allows the player to automatically
		refuse one of the pig's advances and gain +1 Pig's Respect. -->
		
		<<farm_gen pig>>

		<span class="teal">You recognize a <<farm_text pig>> who was particularly helpful.</span>
		<br><br>
		
		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> reaches your
		waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"Reward?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It hesitates, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"H-hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<</if>>
			so I wanted to give <<farm_him pig>> a reward! Next time, if you help me even more, I-I could do it with you instead."
			You release <<farm_him pig>>.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all
				eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask mister <<farm_text pig>> here for tips."
				You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all
				eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask missus <<farm_text pig>> here for tips."
				You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<</if>>
			so <<farm_he pig>> gets to have some fun. If you want me too, then I'll need you on your best behavior."
			You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<<farm_He pig>> mounts you.
		<br><br>

		<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are impressed by your discernment.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<br><br>
		
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: true,
				helpfulPigGender: $farm_work.pig.gender,
				currentConsensual: true,
				pigsLeft: 4,
				demeanor: "submissive",
				location: "woodland",
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="teal">You have a hard time telling them apart,</span> and end up selecting one who looks vaguely familiar.
		<br><br>

		<<farm_gen pig>>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> crawls up to
		your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"For me?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It presses against you, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"H-hey!" you say. "Thanks a lot for helping me today. I want to show you how much I appreciate it. Next time,
			if you help me even more, I-I could do it with you instead." You release <<farm_him pig>> from your legs.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were pretty helpful today.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, I'm letting mister <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want join in, you'd better start helping too!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, I'm letting missus <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want join in, you'd better start helping too!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were fairly helpful today, and I know you all want a reward.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, mister <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, missus <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<</if>>
			If you want me too, then I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<<farm_He pig>> mounts you.
		<br><br>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around to watch you.
		<br><br>
		
		<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte 5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 1>>
		<<elseif $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 2>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 3>>
		<</if>>
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: false,
				helpfulPigGender: $farm_work.pig.gender,
				currentConsensual: true,
				pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
				demeanor: "submissive",
				location: "woodland",
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"But..." You look into your basket. "But these are mine."
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"Hmpf. You want these?" You wave around your basket. "Find them yourself."
	<<else>>
		 "Sorry, but these are mine." You guard your basket.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		Another <<farm_text pig>> responds. "Stupid human. Not ask you, we take. You satisfy."
	<<else>>
		Your response only aggravates them. They advance on you, uncaring.
	<</if>>
	They block your escape. You're deep in the woodland. There's nowhere to run.
	<br><br>

	<!-- Good luck. -->
	<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			rewardHelpful: false,
			helpfulPigGender: "m",
			currentConsensual: false,
			pigsLeft: 5,
			demeanor: "defiant",
			location: "woodland",
			trueConsensual: false
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Forage Reward
<<set _rewardType to $phase.type>>
<<set _rewardQuantity to $phase.quantity>>
<<effects>>

<<farm_gen pig>>

<!-- rewardType can be "potato", "carrot", "apple", "body", or "nothing" -->
<!-- Reward Tradeoffs:
	Potato
		Pros: Can be grown in bulk and gives bonus Respect (+3).
		Cons: Requires a LOT of potatoes to satisfy the pigs.
			Takes a long time (20 min).
			Counts as a feeding action, and is disabled if the pigs are already fully fed.
	Carrot
		Pros: Can be grown in bulk.
			Needs less food that potatoes.
			Takes a short time (10 min).
		Cons: Only gives a small amount (+1) of Respect.
	Apple
		Pros: Gives bonus Respect if the player has a good Housekeeping and Maths Skills (1-3 Respect in total).
			Needs much less food than potatoes.
		Cons: Must be manually gathered from the Forest.
			The time taken varies based on the amount of Respect gained (10-20 minutes in total).
	Body
		Pros: No food loss.
			A skill check can be passed to give +1 Respect.
			The pigs give up to +3 Respect at low Respect.
		Cons: The pigs only give +1 Respect at high Respect.
			Refusing or fighting off a pig at any point will make the following encounters non-consensual.
	Nothing
		Pros: No food loss. Gives you -3 Pig's Respect.
		Cons: Nothing. You should keep doing it :)
	-->
<!-- The in-game name of "carrot" is "wild_carrot".
	Quantities for "body" and "nothing" will be 0. -->
<<if _rewardType is "potato" or _rewardType is "carrot" or _rewardType is "apple">>
	<<if _rewardType is "carrot">>
		<<set _rewardIcon to "wild_carrot">>
	<<else>>
		<<set _rewardIcon to _rewardType>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
		"W-would you all want some <<pluralise 2 _rewardType>>?" you ask.
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		You think about what you have stocked. "Want some <<pluralise 2 _rewardType>>?"
	<<else>>
		 "How about some <<pluralise 2 _rewardType>>?" you say.
	<</if>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		"Food?" "Reward"? "_rewardType?" "Food?" "<<pShe>> give?" "Reward?"
	<<else>>
		They oink to each other.
	<</if>>
	<<switch _rewardType>>
		<<case "potato">>
			You think they recognized the word "potato." They start shuffling back to the farm.
		<<case "carrot">>
			You think they recognized the word "carrot." They start walking back to the farm.
		<<case "apple">>
			You think they recognized the word "apple." They start trotting back to the farm.
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	After leaving the woodland, you head to the storehouse.

	<<switch _rewardType>>
		<<case "potato">>
			You fill your basket with potatoes, then pour them into the pen. You have to make several trips, the
			<<farm_text_many pig>> hungry from all of the exertion. By the end, they rest on their sides.
			<<set $farm_work.pigs_fed += 1>><<physique 2>>
			<br><br>

			<span class="green">You think they found it filling.</span><<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 3>>
			<<pass 20>>
		<<case "carrot">>
			You fill your basket with carrots, then pour them into the pen. You make a few trips, the <<farm_text_many pig>>
			crunching them for longer than you think is necessary. When they're done, they wander away from the fence.
			<<physique 1>>
			<br><br>
			
			<span class="green">You think they enjoyed the snack.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
			<<pass 10>>
		<<case "apple">>
			You fill your basket with apples and head back to the pen, a small crowd having formed by the fence.
			You're worried they may injure themselves if you just pour them in, so you try to split them
			evenly.
			<br><br>

			<!-- The Apple Strudel recipe requires the player to cut apples, and needs Housekeeping Level 2 (aka
				Housekeeping C) to learn it.

				Accurately cutting the apples so that each pig gets roughly the same amount will require a Maths Skill
				of A, because the player will need to estimate the fraction of each apple to give to each pig. -->
			<<if currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400 and $mathstrait gte 3>>
				You spend some time counting up the <<farm_text_many pig>> because they keep moving around.
				You then cut the apples so that
				<span class="teal">each <<farm_text_neutral pig>> gets roughly the same amount.</span>
				<br><br>

				<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are very happy with your efforts.</span><<ggrespect>><<farm_pigs 3>>
				<!-- Takes extra time to feed them properly. -->
				<<pass 10>>
			<<elseif currentSkillValue("housekeeping") gte 400>>
				You try to count how many <<farm_text_many pig>> there are, <span class="teal">but the math makes you dizzy.</span>
				You settle for an estimate instead. By the time you're nearly done, you realize your pieces were
				a little <<if random(1, 2) is 1>> too small. <<else>> too large. <</if>>
				<br><br>

				<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> appreciate your efforts.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 2>>
				<!-- Takes a little extra time to cut the pieces. -->
				<<pass 5>>
			<<else>>
				You're worried about <span class="teal">cutting yourself with a the kitchen knife,</span> so you hand
				them out individually. Some <<farm_text_many pig>> inevitably get less than others.
				<br><br>

				<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> root around for leftovers.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
			<</if>>
			<<pass 10>>
	<</switch>>
	<br><br>

	By the end, you feed them a total of
	<span class="green"><<foodstufficon _rewardIcon>> _rewardQuantity <<pluralise _rewardQuantity _rewardType>>.</span>
	<br><br>

<<elseif _rewardType is "body">>
	<!-- Should not be possible to reach this branch without bestiality being enabled or the farm pigs being monsters. -->
	<!-- Player will satisfy a pig with their body (+1 Pig's Respect). If the player has good Science and Tending,
		they will recognize and reward a pig that was particularly helpful (+1 Pig's Respect). -->
	You look among the <<farm_text_many pig>> gathered before you, deciding which one you'll reward.
	<br><br>

	<!-- Player should have a 50% of passing the Science check with a Science Grade of A. -->
	<<set _rewardBodyChecks to [
		{checkType: "science", checkMin: 600, checkMax: 800},
		{checkType: "tending", checkMin: 600, checkMax: 800, includeBurden: false}
	]>>
	<<eventChecks _rewardBodyChecks>>
	<!-- Going to hell for this lol -->
	<<if _checkResults[0] is 2 and _checkResults[1] is 2>>
		<!-- Extra point of Respect if the player passes both checks. Passing this also allows the player to refuse one
			pig's advances without losing Pig's Respect. -->

		<<farm_gen pig>>

		<span class="teal">You recognize a <<farm_text pig>> who was particularly helpful.</span>
		<br><br>
		
		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> reaches your
		waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"Reward?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It hesitates, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"H-hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> helped me a lot today,
			<</if>>
			so I wanted to give <<farm_him pig>> a reward! Next time, if you help me even more, I-I could do it with you instead."
			You release <<farm_him pig>>.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all
				eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask mister <<farm_text pig>> here for tips."
				You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> here was very helpful today, so <<farm_he pig>> gets a big reward. Me! I saw you all
				eyeing me in the forest, so if you want join in, you'd better ask missus <<farm_text pig>> here for tips."
				You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				"Mister <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<<else>>
				"Missus <<farm_text pig>> was very helpful today,
			<</if>>
			so <<farm_he pig>> gets to have some fun. If you want me too, then I'll need you on your best behavior."
			You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<<farm_He pig>> mounts you.
		<br><br>

		<span class="green">The <<farm_text_many pig>> are impressed by your discernment.</span><<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<br><br>
		
		<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte 5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 1>>
		<<elseif $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 2>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 3>>
		<</if>>

		<!-- This is the only instance of non-forced consensual sex betwen the player and a pig, where the player
			actually has the option to ask them to stop. -->
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: true,
				helpfulPigGender: $farm_work.pig.gender,
				currentConsensual: true,
				pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
				demeanor: "submissive",
				location: "treeline",
				trueConsensual: true
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<span class="teal">You have a hard time telling them apart,</span> and end up selecting one who looks vaguely familiar.
		<br><br>

		<<farm_gen pig>>

		You close your basket and lie against it, guiding <<farm_him pig>> towards you. When <<farm_he pig>> crawls up to
		your waist, you hold <<farm_him pig>> there with your legs.
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>"For me?" <<farm_he pig>> asks.<<else>>It presses against you, unsure of your intentions.<</if>>
		<<deviancy5>>

		You address the rest of the <<farm_text_many pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
			"H-hey!" you say. "Thanks a lot for helping me today. I want to show you how much I appreciate it. Next time,
			if you help me even more, I-I could do it with you instead." You release <<farm_him pig>> from your legs.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were pretty helpful today.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, I'm letting mister <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want join in, you'd better start helping too!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, I'm letting missus <<farm_text pig>> here show you my thank you gift. I saw you all eyeing me in the
				forest, so if you want join in, you'd better start helping too!" You pull <<farm_him pig>> onto you.
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			"Hey!" you say. "You all were fairly helpful today, and I know you all want a reward.
			<<if $farm_work.pig.gender is "m">>
				As thanks, mister <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<<else>>
				As thanks, missus <<farm_text pig>> and I will be putting on a show.
			<</if>>
			If you want me too, then I'll need you on your best behavior." You spread your legs.
		<</if>>
		<<farm_He pig>> mounts you.
		<br><br>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around to watch you.
		<br><br>
		
		<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte 5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 1>>
		<<elseif $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 2>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _pigsLeft to 3>>
		<</if>>
		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: false,
				helpfulPigGender: $farm_work.pig.gender,
				currentConsensual: true,
				pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
				demeanor: "submissive",
				location: "treeline",
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $farm.beasts.pigs gte -5 or not ($settings.bestialityEnabled or $farm_work.pig.monster)>>
		<<farm_pigs -3>>
		They consider you, then snort and trot away.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		They consider you, then snort and trot away.
		<br><br>

		<<farm_gen pig>>

		As they do, a <<farm_text pig>> stays behind.
		
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Stupid human need breed."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Stupid human reward."
			<<else>>
				"No reward. Lie," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Stupid human can satisfy."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> growls at you, blocking your path.
		<</if>>

		The <<farm_text_many pig>> turn around at the sound of <<farm_his pig>> voice. You try to move around <<farm_him pig>>,
		but <<farm_he pig>> moves between you and the farm. You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> don't try to
		stop you, but they also don't try to stop the <<farm_text pig>>.
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: false,
				helpfulPigGender: "m",
				currentConsensual: false,
				pigsLeft: 3,
				demeanor: "defiant",
				location: "treeline",
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Pigs Reward
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _rewardHelpful to $phase.rewardHelpful>>
<<set _helpfulPigGender to $phase.helpfulPigGender>>
<<set _currentConsensual to $phase.currentConsensual>>
<<set _pigsLeft to $phase.pigsLeft>>
<<set _demeanor to $phase.demeanor>>
<<set _location to $phase.location>>
<<set _trueConsensual to $phase.trueConsensual>>

<<if $sexstart is 1>>
	<<set $sexstart to 0>>
	<<if _location is "treeline">>
		<span class="green">You are at the edge of the woodland. Alex might be able to hear you.</span>
		<br><br>
	<<elseif _location is "woodland">>
		<span class="red">You are deep in the woodland. Alex will not be able to hear your cries.</span>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Reward): Invalid location "_location". Please report.
	<</if>>

	<<if _currentConsensual>>
		<<deviancy5>>
	<</if>>

	<<if _currentConsensual>>
		<<consensual>>
		<<set $consensual to 1>>
		<<neutral 1>>
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
	<<else>>
		<<set $consensual to 0>>
		<<controlloss>>
		<<violence 1>>
		<<neutral 1>>
		<<molested>>
	<</if>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals monster>>
	<<else>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals beast>>
	<</if>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	
	<<if _location is "treeline" and Time.betweenHours(5, 20)>>
		<<enable_rescue>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $rescue to 0>>
	<</if>>

	<<farm_trust pig>>

	<!-- Submissive start has no change.
		Defiant starts with increased Anger and decreased Trust.-->
	<<if _demeanor is "defiant">>
		<<set $enemyanger += 40>>
		<<set $enemytrust -= 40>>
	<</if>>

	<<if _trueConsensual>>
		<<set $noFinish to 0>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $noFinish to 1>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br>

<<if _currentConsensual>>The other <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you, eager to see you moan.
<<else>>The other <<farm_text_many pig>> crowd around you, eager to see you squeal.
<</if>>

<!-- Fungi stealing checks for if the player non-consensually "rewards" the pigs deep in the woodland. -->
<<if _location is "woodland" and _currentConsensual is false>>
<!-- Player effectively loses 0.6 fungi per turn. -->
	<<for _i = 0; _i < 3; _i++>>
		<<if (_basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0) and random(1, 5) is 1>>
			<<if (_basket[1] is 0) or (_basket[0] gt 0 and _basket[1] gt 0 and random(1, 2) is 1)>>
				<<set _foodTarget to "mushroom">>
				<<set _basket[0] -= 1>>
				<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= 1>>
			<<else>>
				<<set _foodTarget to "truffle">>
				<<set _basket[1] -= 1>>
				<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= 1>>
			<</if>>

			<<if $farm_work["pig"].monster>>
				A <<if random(1, 2) is 1>> pigboy <<else>> piggirl <</if>> munches on a _foodTarget from your basket.
			<<else>>
				A pig munches on a _foodTarget from your basket.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>
	<</for>>
<</if>>

<br><br>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Finish]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
			helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
			currentConsensual: _currentConsensual,
			pigsLeft: _pigsLeft - 1,
			location: _location,
			trueConsensual: _trueConsensual
		}>>
	<</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
			helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
			currentConsensual: _currentConsensual,
			pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
			demeanor: _demeanor,
			location: _location,
			trueConsensual: _trueConsensual
		}>>
	<</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Finish
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _rewardHelpful to $phase.rewardHelpful>>
<<set _helpfulPigGender to $phase.helpfulPigGender>>
<<set _currentConsensual to $phase.currentConsensual>>
<<set _pigsLeft to $phase.pigsLeft>>
<<set _location to $phase.location>>

<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>

	The <<farm_text pig>> climbs off you, satisfied.

	<!-- +Respect if done consensually. -Respect if nonconsensual. -->
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		The others cheer.
		<br>
		
		<<if _currentConsensual>>
			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"<<pShe>> so breedable."
			<<else>>
				"You see <<phim>> face?"
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"You should been rougher."
			<<else>>
				"Can be rougher next time."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"Can we keep <<phim>>?"
			<<else>>
				"We can breed more if want stay."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"Not so great now."
			<<else>>
				"I hope <<pshe>> know place."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"You should been rougher."
			<<else>>
				"Can be rougher next time."
			<</if>>
			<br>

			<<if random(1, 2) is 2>>
				"We keep <<phim>> here?"
			<<else>>
				"I bet <<pshe>> like that."
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		The others crowd around it. They sniff and lick it, then turn back to you.
	<</if>>
	<!-- +Respect if done consensually. -Respect if nonconsensual. -->
	<<if _currentConsensual>>
		<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
	<<else>>
		<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you try to push yourself back up.

	<<farm_gen pig>>

	<<if _pigsLeft gte 1>>
		As you do, another <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.

		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Reward too little."
			<<else>>
				"Reward too few," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfied."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> paws at the ground. You can tell <<farm_he pig>> also wants to mate.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<if _rewardHelpful>>
			<<set _rewardHelpful to false>>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster and _helpfulPigGender is "m">>
				The pigboy you had sex with moves to block <<farm_him pig>>. "No. You not helpful. No reward."
			<<elseif $farm_work.pig.monster and _helpfulPigGender is "f">>
				The piggirl you had sex with moves to block <<farm_him pig>>. "No. You not helpful. No reward."
			<<else>>
				The pig you had sex with moves to block it. Your pig growls.
			<</if>>

			The <<farm_text_many pig>> stare at each other. They lunge at each other and start wrestling on the
			ground. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> watch in silence.
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Fight]]>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
					helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
					currentConsensual: _currentConsensual,
					pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
					location: _location,
					trueConsensual: false
				}>>
			<</link>>
		<<else>>
			You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> seem just as lustful. How many more will you need to satisfy?
			<br><br>

			<<if _currentConsensual and hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
				<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
					<<set $phase to {
						basket: _basket,
						rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
						helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
						currentConsensual: true,
						pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
						demeanor: "submissive",
						location: _location,
						trueConsensual: false
					}>>
				<</link>><<deviant5>>
			<br>
			<</if>>

			<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
					helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
					currentConsensual: false,
					pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
					demeanor: "defiant",
					location: _location,
					trueConsensual: false
				}>>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		They don't stop you.
		<<if _location is "treeline" and _currentConsensual>>
			You grab your basket and start walking back towards the farm.
		<<elseif _location is "woodland" and _currentConsensual>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<!-- Pigs only rest for 5 minutes if satisfied sexually. -->
			<<pass 5>>
			<!-- Grand Pig Conspiracy when? -->
			Done with fucking you, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze about on the earth. Looking around, it's clear you only
			had sex with a small number of those who had gathered here.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">You wonder why they seem so organized.</span><<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up.
			<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] is 0>>
				Some <<farm_text_many pig>> approach you during this time, giving you a lick or a nuzzle for the meal.
			<</if>>
			A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes, but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from
			approaching.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span><<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>			
				<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] is 0>>
					"Body good, thank for meal," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
				<<else>>
					"Body good," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We go back now." You follow them.
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. You follow them.
			<</if>>
		<<elseif _location is "treeline">>
			You grab your basket and stagger back towards the farm.
		<<else>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<!-- Pigs only rest for 5 minutes if satisfied sexually. -->
			<<pass 5>>
			<span class="red">You ache all over.</span><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>
			
			Done with fucking you, the <<farm_text_many pig>> laze about on the earth. Looking around, it's clear you only
			had sex with a small number of those who had gathered here.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">You wonder why they seem so organized.</span><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>

			You don't know the way back, so you wait for them to get up. A few of them still look at you with lustful eyes,
			but the others form a ring of sorts that stops them from approaching.
			<br><br>

			<span class="red">It seems like they think you've paid your due.</span><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>

			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>			
				<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] is 0>>
					"Thank for meal, fucktoy," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We leave." You follow them.
				<<else>>
					"Fucktoy learn good lesson," a <<farm_text pig>> says. "We leave." You follow them.
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				Eventually, they get up and start trotting somewhere. They leer at you as they go. You follow them.
			<</if>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

<!-- Fighting off the pig will remove the option for consensual sex. -->
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	The <<farm_text pig>> backs away from you, cowed. The others make room after seeing how you fought.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you try to push yourself back up.

	<<farm_gen pig>>

	<<if _pigsLeft gte 1>>
		As you do, another <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.

		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
				"Not enough. Not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
			<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
				"More breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Too pretty."
			<<else>>
				"Too pretty," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfied."
			<</if>>
		<<else>>
			<<farm_He pig>> paws at the ground. 
		<</if>>
		Despite your display, you can tell <<farm_he pig>> thinks you're worth the risk.
		<br><br>

		You look around. The other <<farm_text_many pig>> seem just as lustful. How many more will you need to fight off?
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
				helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
				currentConsensual: false,
				pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
				demeanor: "defiant",
				location: _location,
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		<<if _location is "treeline">>
			They don't stop you. You grab your basket and start walking back towards the farm.
			<br><br>
		<<else>>
			<<set _passTime to random(30, 40)>>
			<<pass _passTime>>
			<!-- Pigs immediately flee to the farm if they are fought off, but since they don't directly guide the
				player back, the player needs to spend some extra time orienting themselves. -->
			The <<farm_text_many pig>> have had enough of your violence. One runs away. You clench your fist. Another flees.
			And then another. Soon, only stragglers remain. Most of the <<farm_text_many pig>> flee in the same direction.
			You suspect they're running back to the farm. You follow them.
			<br><br>

			<!-- Tending skill of B. -->
			You come across many different animal tracks on your way back.
			<<if $sciencetrait gte 3>>
				<span class="green">You remember your lessons from science class.</span>
				You follow the pig prints back to the farm.					
			<<else>>
				<<pass 20>>
				The indents all look the same. You spend some time going in circles, until at last, you see some familiar
				buildings through the treeline.
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			Throughout it all, you find yourself wondering what exactly just happened.
			<br><br>

			Where did they take you?<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			
			Why were they so organized?<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>

			Does anyone know?<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>
			<br><br>

			Would anyone believe you?<<gstress>><<stress 6>>
			<br><br>
		<</if>>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<<elseif $alarm is 1 and $rescue gte 1>><<set $rescued += 1>>
	"I'm coming!" It's Alex. The <<farm_text_many pig>> back away from you at the sound. They start fleeing into the
	undergrowth.<<llrespect>><<farm_pigs -3>>
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<npc Alex>><<person1>>
	Alex arrives at the edge of the woodland, and laughs. <<He>> pushes through the foliage, and helps you to your feet.
	"Pigs can be like that," <<he>> says. "If all else fails, don't be afraid to lay down the law."

	<<if $exposed gte 1>>
		<<glust>><<npcincr Alex lust 1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<!-- Consensual "Ask to stop" edge case. Honestly such an edge case that you could make an argument that there
		should be a Feat awarded for achieving it. Would be relatively easy to achieve though. Just obscure. -->
	The <<farm_text pig>> slowly climbs off of you.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<farm_He pig>> whines. "Why no mate? I good. We good. Help you."
	<<else>>
		It whines. It paws at your leg, pleading with its eyes.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you push yourself off the ground.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>
	
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		As you walk away, the other pigpeople jeer at you.
	<<else>>
		As you walk away, you hear squeals and oinks behind you.
	<</if>>
	It's clear you've agitated them.<<llrespect>><<farm_pigs -3>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>


<!-- There is a potential bug where the player rewards the helpful pig in the Woodland, while there is only
	1 pig left to satisfy. This would cause the helpful pig to save the player, and the text would say the
	player is able to walk out of the Woodland on their own. This situation is currently impossible because
	the "Farm Woodland Forage Reward Extreme" event starts at 4 unsatisfied pigs, and the "helpfulPig" event
	can only triggers one time after the first pig is satisfied. However, if the Woodland events get changed
	in the future, this edge case may need need to be handled. -->
:: Farm Woodland Pigs Reward Fight
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _rewardHelpful to $phase.rewardHelpful>>
<<set _helpfulPigGender to $phase.helpfulPigGender>>
<<set _currentConsensual to $phase.currentConsensual>>
<<set _pigsLeft to $phase.pigsLeft>>
<<set _location to $phase.location>>

<!-- Your pig has a 40% chance of winning you the +Respect and -pigsLeft. Your power of horni fills it with determination!
	Unfortunately it just had sex with you, and you milked it RATHER good. -->
<<if random(1, 5) lte 3>>
	At last, the other <<farm_text pig>> presses your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> into the dirt.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		Panting, <<farm_he pig _helpfulPigGender>> looks up at the other <<farm_text pig>> and squeezes out four words.
		"No... helpful. No... reward."
	<<else>>
		It looks tired, struggling underneath the other pig, but still finds rooms in its lungs to muster out a whine.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	
	The other <<farm_text_many pig>> look between you and your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>>.
	<<farm_His pig _helpfulPigGender>> loss fills you with a dread for what's come.<<gstress>><<stress 6>>

	<!-- While your horni savior may have lost, their valiant struggle gives them a 50% chance of convincing the other pigs
		to be nicer to you! If you lose the coinflip, #SkillIssue. -->
	<<if random(1, 2) is 1>>
		<<set _pigsLeft -= 1>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<set _pigsLeft -= 1>>
	At last, your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> presses the other <<farm_text pig>> into the dirt.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		Panting, <<farm_he pig _helpfulPigGender>> looks at the other <<farm_text_many pig>> and repeats himself.
		"No helpful. No reward."
	<<else>>
		It looks tired, but still manages a growl towards the other pigs.
	<</if>>
	<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
	<br><br>

	The other <<farm_text_many pig>> look between you and your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>>.
	You can tell your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> is too tired to fight another <<farm_text_neutral pig>>,
	if they insist.
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if _pigsLeft is 0>>
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		They respect <<farm_his pig _helpfulPigGender>> statement.
	<<else>>
		They lose interest.
	<</if>>

	The other <<farm_text_many pig>> start trickling back into the woodland, looking for other things to interest
	them. Picking up your basket, you find your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> standing in front of you.

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		"Good sex," <<farm_he pig _helpfulPigGender>> says. "Wanted to thank."
	<<else>>
		It nuzzles and licks your legs.
	<</if>>
	<<lstress>><<stress -6>>
	<br><br>

	You give your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> a pat on the head, then start heading back towards the farm.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<!-- BROTHER. MAY I HAVE SOME OATS?!?!?! -->
	
	<<farm_gen pig>>

	Another <<farm_text pig>> steps forward.
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
			"Still not enough. Still not satisfy." <<farm_He pig>> says. "Need breed more."
		<<elseif random(1, 2) is 1>>
			"Still more breed," <<farm_he pig>> says. "Reward too little."
		<<else>>
			"Still reward too few," <<farm_he pig>> says. "We not satisfy."
		<</if>>
		The other pigpeople murmur in agreement. Your <<farm_text pig _helpfulPigGender>> looks at you, then moves to
		the side. "Sorry. Tried. Can't protect," <<farm_he pig _helpfulPigGender>> says. <<farm_He pig _helpfulPigGender>>
		watches, remorseful, as the <<farm_text pig>> approaches you.
	<<else>>
		It oinks at your pig, then growls at you. The other pigs growl as well. Your pig looks at you, whining. The other
		pigs begin to growl at it. When the other pig steps towards it, it moves to the side. It looks on, remorseful,
		as the other pig approaches you.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<if _currentConsensual and hasSexStat("deviancy", 5)>>
		<<link [[Submit to them|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
				helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
				currentConsensual: true,
				pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
				demeanor: "submissive",
				location: _location,
				trueConsensual: false
			}>>
		<</link>><<deviant5>>
		<br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Fight <<farm_him pig>> off|Farm Woodland Pigs Reward]]>><<set $sexstart to 1>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			rewardHelpful: _rewardHelpful,
			helpfulPigGender: _helpfulPigGender,
			currentConsensual: false,
			pigsLeft: _pigsLeft,
			demeanor: "defiant",
			location: _location,
			trueConsensual: false
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Scold
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<set _startPosition to $phase.startPosition>>
<<effects>>

<<if $tendingSuccess>>
	<<if _startPosition is "standing">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			"Away!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span>
			The <<farm_text pig>> releases you, and goes back to foraging among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<else>>
			"Down!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span>
			The pig drops to the ground, and goes back to rooting among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _startPosition is "prone">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			"Away!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span>
			The <<farm_text pig>> backs away from you, and goes back to foraging among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<else>>
			"Back!" you say, <span class="green">your voice firm and sure.</span>
			The pig backs away from you, and goes back to rooting among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Scold): Invalid startPosition "_startPosition".
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<if (_startPosition is "prone") or ($farm.beasts.pigs lt -5 and $rng gte 51)>>
		<<if _startPosition is "standing">>
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"A-away!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the <<farm_text pig>> pays you no heed.
				<<farm_He pig>> pulls you to the ground.<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<<else>>
				"D-down!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the pig pays you no heed.
				It forces you to the ground.<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Rape]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
					forageType: _forageType,
					startPosition: _startPosition,
					pigTracker: []
				}>>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
				"A-away!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the <<farm_text pig>> pays you no heed.
				<<farm_He pig>> climbs on top of you.
				<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<<else>>
				"D-down!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the pig pays you no heed.
				It climbs on top of you.<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
			<</if>>
			<br><br>

			<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Rape]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>>
				<<set $phase to {
					basket: _basket,
					remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
					forageType: _forageType,
					startPosition: _startPosition,
					pigTracker: []
				}>>
			<</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			"A-away!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the <<farm_text pig>> pays you no heed.
			<<farm_He pig>> humps you for a few moments, before tiring and stepping away. It goes back to foraging among the trees.
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<<else>>
			"D-down!" you say, but <span class="red">your voice shakes,</span> and the pig pays you no heed.
			It humps you for a few moments, before tiring and dropping to the ground. It goes back to rooting among the trees.
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
				forageType: _forageType
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Pigs Shove
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<set _startPosition to $phase.startPosition>>
<<effects>>

<<if $physiqueSuccess>>
	<<if _startPosition is "standing">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<span class="green">You shove the <<farm_text pig>> away from you.</span>
			<<farm_He pig>> steps away and and goes back to foraging among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="green">You shove the pig away from you.</span>
			It drops to the ground and and goes back to rooting among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
				forageType: _forageType
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif _startPosition is "prone">>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			<span class="green">You shove the <<farm_text pig>> off of you.</span>
			Surprised by your strength, <<farm_he pig>> goes back to foraging among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<<else>>
			<span class="green">You shove the pig off of you.</span>
			Surprised by your strength, it goes back to rooting among the trees.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
				forageType: _forageType
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Shove): Invalid startPosition "_startPosition".
	<</if>>

<<else>>
	<<if (_startPosition is "prone") or ($farm.beasts.pigs lt -5 and $rng gte 51)>>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			You try to shove the <<farm_text pig>> off of you, <span class="red">but <<farm_he pig>> wrestles back
			and forces you back to the ground.</span>
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<gpain>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>><<violence 1>>
		<<else>>
			You try to shove the pig off of you, <span class="red">but it's too heavy. It forces you back to the ground.</span>
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Rape]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
				forageType: _forageType,
				startPosition: _startPosition,
				pigTracker: []
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>

	<<else>>
		<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
			You try to shove the <<farm_text pig>> away from you, <span class="red">but <<farm_he pig>> wrestles back
			and holds your arms behind you.</span> <<farm_he pig>> humps you for a few moments, before tiring and stepping away.
			It goes back to foraging among the trees.<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<<else>>
			You try to shove the pig away from you, <span class="red">but it's too heavy.</span> It humps you for a few moments,
			before tiring and dropping to the ground. It goes back to rooting among the trees.
			<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>><<gtrauma>><<gstress>><<trauma 6>><<stress 6>>
		<</if>>
		<br><br>

		<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
			<<set $phase to {
				basket: _basket,
				remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
				forageType: _forageType
			}>>
		<</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
<</if>>


<!-- Should not be possible while player is "prone". -->
:: Farm Woodland Pigs Endure
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<effects>>

<<if $farm.beasts.pigs lt -5 and $rng gte 51>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		You endure as the <<farm_text pig>> humps you. Unsatisfied, <<farm_he pig>> wrestles you to the ground.
	<<else>>
		You endure as the pig humps you. Its weight forces you to the ground.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Rape]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType,
			startPosition: "standing",
			pigTracker: []
		}>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>
	<br>

<<else>>
	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		You endure as the <<farm_text pig>> humps you. <<farm_He pig>> soon tires, and steps away.
		<<farm_He pig>> goes back to foraging among the trees.
	<<else>>
		You endure as the pig humps you. It soon tires, or is otherwise satisfied, and drops to the ground.
		It goes back to rooting among the trees.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>

<</if>>

:: Farm Woodland Pigs Hand
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<set _startPosition to $phase.startPosition>>
<<if $sexstart is 1>>
	<<set $sexstart to 0>>
	<span class="red">You are deep in the woodland. Alex will not be able to hear your cries.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<consensual>>
	<<set $consensual to 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals monster>>
	<<else>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals beast>>
	<</if>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<set $rescue to 0>>
	<<farm_trust pig>>

	<<if _startPosition is "standing">>
		You reach back and feel beneath the <<farm_text pig>>.
		<<npchand>><<deviancy3>>
	<<elseif _startPosition is "prone">>
		You reach up and feel beneath the <<farm_text pig>>.
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
		<<npchand>><<deviancy4>>
	<<else>>
		ERROR (Farm Woodland Pigs Hand): Invalid startPosition: "_startPosition"
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br><br>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand Finish]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Farm Woodland Pigs Hand]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>


:: Farm Woodland Pigs Hand Finish
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<effects>>

<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>

	Satisfied, the <<farm_text pig>> trots away.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you push yourself off the ground.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>

<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	Sufficiently cowed, the <<farm_text pig>> drops to the ground and scurries away.<<grespect>><<farm_pigs 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you push yourself off the ground.

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	The <<farm_text pig>> trots away with a huff.<<lrespect>><<farm_pigs -1>>
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you push yourself off the ground.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Continue|Farm Woodland Forage]]>>
		<<set $phase to {
			basket: _basket,
			remainingAttempts: _remainingAttempts,
			forageType: _forageType
		}>>
	<</link>>
	<br>

<</if>>


<!-- If the player is getting raped and the encounter is nonconsensual, pigs will have a chance of being attracted
	to the noise. Each turn, each pig will have a chance of stealing a Mushroom or Truffle from the player's basket.
	
	Player gains an average of 10 mushrooms or truffles every 20 minutes, and at the end, may potentially be raped.
	Math should work out so that the player loses around 1/5 of their basket if they take longer than 10 turns.
	However, the increasing number of pigs should cause them to lose everything by turn 20.

	Napkin Math:
		A pig has a 20% chance of appearing each turn.
		Each pig has a 20% chance of stealing a mushroom each turn.
	
	Turn 0: 0 pigs, 0 mushrooms lost
	Turn 5: 1 pig, 0 mushrooms lost
	Turn 10: 2 pigs, 1 mushrooms lost
	Turn 15: 3 pigs, 3 mushrooms lost
	Turn 20: 4 pigs, 6 mushrooms lost
	Turn 25: 5 pigs, 10 mushrooms lost
	etc. -->
:: Farm Woodland Pigs Rape
<<set _basket to $phase.basket>>
<<set _remainingAttempts to $phase.remainingAttempts>>
<<set _forageType to $phase.forageType>>
<<set _startPosition to $phase.startPosition>>
<<set _pigTracker to $phase.pigTracker>>
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<span class="red">You are deep in the woodland. Alex will not be able to hear your cries.</span>
	<br><br>

	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>

	<<if $farm_work.pig.monster>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals monster>>
	<<else>>
		<<beastNEWinit 1 pig $farm_work.pig.gender $farm_work.pig.genitals beast>>
	<</if>>
	<<beastCombatInit>>
	<<set $rescue to 0>>
	<<if _startPosition is "prone">>
		<<set $position to "missionary">>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>
<<alarmstate>>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br>
<!-- Truffle eaters go here. -->
<<if _pigTracker.length is 0>>
	Your basket lays at your side. No other <<farm_text_many pig>> are nearby.
<<elseif _pigTracker.length is 1>>
	<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0>>
		A <<farm_text pig>> glances between you and your basket.
	<<else>>
		A <<farm_text pig>> watches you, sad that your basket is empty.
	<</if>>
<<elseif _pigTracker.length is 2>>
	<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0>>
		A pair of <<farm_text_many pig>> look between you and your basket.
	<<else>>
		A pair of <<farm_text_many pig>> watch you, sad that your basket is empty.
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if _basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0>>
		A small group of <<farm_text_many pig>> snack from your basket while they watch.
	<<else>>
		A small group of <<farm_text_many pig>> watch you, sad that your basket is empty.
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

<!-- Pig stealing checks -->
<<for _i = 0; _i < _pigTracker.length; _i++>>
	<!-- Manually coded genders for the pigpeople because I'm not sure if there's a macro to do this automatically.  -->
	<<if (_basket[0] + _basket[1] gt 0) and random(1, 5) is 1>>
		<<if (_basket[1] is 0) or (_basket[0] gt 0 and _basket[1] gt 0 and random(1, 2) is 1)>>
			<<set _foodTarget to "mushroom">>
			<<set _basket[0] -= 1>>
			<<set $foodstuff["mushroom"].amount -= 1>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _foodTarget to "truffle">>
			<<set _basket[1] -= 1>>
			<<set $foodstuff["truffle"].amount -= 1>>
		<</if>>

		<<if $farm_work["pig"].monster>>
			A <<if _pigTracker[_i] is "m">> pigboy <<else>> piggirl <</if>> munches on a _foodTarget from your basket.
		<<else>>
			A pig munches on a _foodTarget from your basket.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<</for>>

<!-- Pig generation checks -->
<<if random(1, 5) is 1>>
	<<if $farm_work["pig"].monster>>
		<<if random(1, 2) is 1>>
			A pigboy pokes his head out of the treeline. He glances between you and your basket.
